<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gagik-Abas of Kars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1029–<a href="/years/1065">1065</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gagik-Abas was the last king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kars">Kars</a>, the Armenian Bagratid kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vanand">Vanand</a> in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, reigning from 1029 to 1065. After the Byzantine annexation of Ani in 1045 and the Seljuk sack of the city in 1064, he ceded Kars to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> in exchange for estates in Cappadocia, where he spent his last years.</p></div>
